DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The nneettiissrr kernel interface suite allows device drivers (and other packet
     sources) to direct packets to protocols for directly dispatched or de‐
     ferred processing.  Protocol registration and work stream statistics may
     be monitored using netstat(1).

   PPrroottooccooll rreeggiissttrraattiioonn
     Protocols register and unregister handlers using nneettiissrr__rreeggiisstteerr() and
     nneettiissrr__uunnrreeggiisstteerr(), and may also manage queue limits and statistics us‐
     ing the nneettiissrr__cclleeaarrqqddrrooppss(), nneettiissrr__ggeettqqddrrooppss(), nneettiissrr__ggeettqqlliimmiitt(), and
     nneettiissrr__sseettqqlliimmiitt().

     In case of VIMAGE kernels each virtual network stack (vnet), that is not
     the default base system network stack, calls nneettiissrr__rreeggiisstteerr__vvnneett() and
     nneettiissrr__uunnrreeggiisstteerr__vvnneett() to enable or disable packet processing by the
     nneettiissrr for each protocol.  Disabling will also purge any outstanding
     packet from the protocol queue.

     nneettiissrr supports multi-processor execution of handlers, and relies on a
     combination of source ordering and protocol-specific ordering and work-
     placement policies to decide how to distribute work across one or more
     worker threads.  Registering protocols will declare one of three poli‐
     cies:

     NETISR_POLICY_SOURCE  nneettiissrr should maintain source ordering without ad‐
                           vice from the protocol.  nneettiissrr will ignore any
                           flow IDs present on _m_b_u_f headers for the purposes
                           of work placement.

     NETISR_POLICY_FLOW    nneettiissrr should maintain flow ordering as defined by
                           the _m_b_u_f header flow ID field.  If the protocol im‐
                           plements _n_h___m_2_f_l_o_w, then nneettiissrr will query the pro‐
                           tocol in the event that the _m_b_u_f doesn't have a
                           flow ID, falling back on source ordering.

     NETISR_POLICY_CPU     nneettiissrr will entirely delegate all work placement
                           decisions to the protocol, querying _n_h___m_2_c_p_u_i_d for
                           each packet.

